# Which is heavier? Three surprising pairs
subtitle: "Tap the heavier of three surprising pairs, from a blue whale's heart to a puffy cloud, and see why weight hides in things spread thin."

## Which is heavier? Three surprising pairs
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: rom
      title: Blue whale heart, Royal Ontario Museum
      authors: Royal Ontario Museum / CBC News
      year: 2017
      finding: the plastinated heart of a blue whale stranded in Newfoundland in 2014 weighs about 180 kg
    - id: air
      title: U.S. Standard Atmosphere
      authors: NOAA, NASA, US Air Force
      year: 1976
      finding: air at sea level weighs about 1.2 kg per cubic metre; a 4 × 4 × 2.5 m bedroom holds 40 m³, about 48 kg
    - id: cloud
      title: How much does a cloud weigh?
      authors: Margaret LeMone, National Center for Atmospheric Research (via USGS)
      year: 2016
      url: https://www.usgs.gov/special-topics/water-science-school/science/how-much-does-a-cloud-weigh
      finding: a fair-weather cumulus about 1 km across holds about 500 tonnes of water droplets
    - id: cdc
      title: CDC growth charts
      authors: US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention
      year: 2000
      finding: the median 10-year-old weighs about 32 kg

    cards heavy cites ["rom","air","cloud"] unit kg compare "Which is heavier?" hidden true
